        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:QuadrDed">Quadr Ded</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Quadr Ded 8" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="529" ed="#liebermann"/>Uirtus eciam diffinita est, scientia perceptibilis, naturæ consentanea; infinitum uero malitiæ dedecus et a summa defectus essentia nec sub alternali generatione producitur nec cert[o<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#QuadrDed_8.lnote.oe.6"/>] multitudinis fine concluditur.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 529 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="QuadrDed_8.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">529</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">certa <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">certa <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
